 **The one point of trust** is that the Lean definitions say what this paper says. The certificate prints every definition the statements use and compares it with this paper (its §1.2–§1.3). That comparison is what a reader should check.
 
-**How.** The text of §2–§10 was cut into 68 pieces, each a short self-contained file. Aristotle, an AI system made by Harmonic [Har26], wrote the Lean proofs. On the author's machine each returned project was compared with the previous one, searched for forbidden constructs, and compiled module by module; the main statements of each piece were restated by hand in a check file, and their faithfulness to the paper was audited. At the end all 416 modules were compiled again from their sources, in one clean rebuild, all with exit code 0. The project has 416 Lean files (415 in its 68 folders, and the main file), 60 964 lines and 3 449 theorem and lemma declarations.
